COMPILATION OF: E49A1

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49A1

   1 a 0000 E49A1:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P1] operand inversion of golden/e48p2e/E48E7 [C330].
   4 a 0006      That object's single reading is ambiguous: HL carried the
   5 a 0006      member, which was BOTH the right operand ([C191]'s "HL =
   6 a 0006      right") and the internal cell ([C326]'s wording), and A
   7 a 0006      carried the extent while B carried the literal length, class-
   8 a 0006      and position-readings alike.  Here the member is written on
   9 a 0006      the LEFT; [C330] itself names "the FIXED member on the LEFT of
  10 a 0006      a TEST" as having no object. */
  11 c 0006   dcl
  12 c 0006     1 rec,
  13 c 0006       2 name char(3),
  14 c 0006       2 nxt fixed bin(15);
  15 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  16 c 0006   if rec.name = 'AB' then k = 1;
  17 c 001D   put list('K=', k);
  18 c 003F   stop;
  19 a 0042 end E49A1;

CODE SIZE = 0042
DATA AREA = 000B
FREE SYMS = 3879
END  COMPILATION
